 "notes": [
  "frames[].hex is exact for the header and for DATA. For control frames, implementations MUST decode hex to the same (type, JSON value); their own encoder may order keys or space differently, so encode tests compare decode(encode(x)) == x and parse(json_text) == x, not bytes.",
  "decode_errors[] feed `input` (hex, or a `gen` spec) to a fresh decoder in one buffer. `stage` says which layer must reject it: preface | frame (codec) | data (DATA payload parse) | message (JSON parse of a known control type). `expect` is ok | need_more | bad_preface | bad_length | unknown_type | bad_data | bad_json.",
  "gen spec: {\"header_len\": L, \"type\": T, \"payload_fill\": \"00\", \"payload_len\": N} builds u32 BE L | u8 T | N bytes of fill; DATA gens add slot/offset as the first 10 payload bytes."
 ],
